From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:05:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Surgeon sign-in: only a signed-in transplant surgeon can
 confirm an approval

Step 3 gains a sign-in card. The coordinator bridge (127.0.0.1) checks the
password against pods/alder/staff.json (salted PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, never
leaves Mac A), sets an HttpOnly SameSite=Strict session cookie (20 min idle),
and refuses review.confirmed unless the session is a transplant surgeon
whose name matches the surgeon on the form's QR. The confirmed event carries
approved_by; auth.login/failed/locked/logout lines join the run log, never a
password. Five wrong passwords lock an account for 60 s.

The page's Confirm button follows who is signed in (sign in to confirm,
locked for the wrong role or the wrong person, otherwise Confirm approval);
the bridge checks the same things again. REPLAY pages have no bridge, so
their sign-in is simulated and labelled as such. Typing in the card no
longer drives the deck; Escape closes it; R keeps the session.

bridge/auth.py add|list|remove manages accounts. Seeded demo account:
m.castillo / alder-2026 (Dr. M. Castillo, the surgeon on the forms).
11 new offline tests, including the HTTP gate. web/dist is rebuilt by the
launch scripts (python3 web/build.py).

